+PREPARED C HOT-PLACEMENT DERIVATIVE — 2026-10-30
+
+STATUS AND SCOPE
+
+Prepared supporting-tool C port, not producer-use clearance. Whole actual-source
+independent review is required. No invocation of real Clang/assembler/linker
+producer commands, no source builds, no remote work, no produced target-image
+execution and no timing has occurred using this C port. Local compilation of
+these C support tools and synthetic C controls is development validation only.
+All real production/use remains held by root until its explicit disposition.
+
+Future selected source pair, per root and takeover-state.json:
+  main ce1bea1eeb8ece6db744726875b136fba023d317
+  #883 cecd49628570e28004254a5639f10d74a13d3346
+Current-head CI41057707200 success and separately published qualification137 /
+inventory138 establish only their reported source/host/role scopes. They do not
+supply new 9700X normal images, exact hot-placement proofs or timing evidence.
+The old immutable 6a/b68 archives, 14 images, normal preflights and failed hot
+placement receipts remain unchanged and are not relabeled as this pair.
+
+PROVENANCE
+
+The accepted #502 inside-hot-section method is from performance commit
+  dd92b91a3a98f57b505cc76ea13cbd74d23edffa
+  docs/measurements/checker-placement-502-2026-10-27
+Original link.sh blob e07ad73ed02a584641f9bdb7af8aeb1976c26e8b is retained
+byte-exact under original/link.sh (SHA256
+bf52635dfd78cb5192eaa1f6d7646722546fab34a2ad17d39dc9b5fc0040c3ef).
+Original objects.sh blob d6b5eb37326574655b91a4548dbeb8e932d23dff is retained
+byte-exact under original/objects.sh (SHA256
+f72d926dc35dc1b129b4fc5e2e6544e4d0425936e12eb7f040a725bfb245ff46).
+These are provenance, not new executable orchestration. C replaces old eval /
+first-line flag scraping with the current build.sh NUL APIs and exact pinned
+reference arrays. The ordinary external-pad method and failed evidence remain
+untouched. No production feature flag or source semantics is introduced.
+
+Python frozen b0 and the later unreviewed driver refresh are separately retained
+under ../python-prototype-history/. The 100 Python controls are development
+history only; neither they nor the old Python review qualify this C port.
+This C implementation carries the logic findings and environment/driver fixes,
+with its own source hashes, controls, statuses and actual-code review.
+
+FILES AND GATES
+
+hp_method.c is the non-timing C controller. It only invokes existing Bash APIs,
+the pinned Clang driver, pinned Wild through that driver, and /usr/bin/sha256sum.
+Every producer child is execv argv (no shell evaluation), with exclusive raw
+NUL argv, split stdout/stderr and actual exit-status artifacts. Parallel source
+compiles are bounded by sched_getaffinity / distinct core_cpus_list groups;
+new work stops upon observed failure and all live wrappers are waited. Original
+source order controls final link order regardless of compile completion order.
+
+Before producer probes, require canonical inputs, full qualified source-manifest
+validation, exact qualified normal-image SHA, inherited shared-host lock and
+pinned official Clang23.1.4/license/Wild hashes. New outputs are fresh and
+outside the source tree. The source manifest must contain build.sh and every
+API translation unit; the owner must supply the complete qualified archive
+manifest, including included headers/support code. The controller does not
+infer a full dependency graph from C text.
+
+hp_common.c removes include/library/driver/preload overrides in its private
+process environment, sets task-private tool/resource paths and explicit source
+mode, and retains full selected environment via toolchain-environment.nul.
+No global environment or settings are changed. HELD is checked, never invented.
+The default target and successful effective C/assembler driver receipts bind
+canonical Clang identity, exact triple, CPU and full ordered feature vector.
+The assembler gets only the explicit pinned target/ISA and assembly operands;
+C-only -D/-I/-f/-W flags remain on C commands. Direct C and -S use identical
+qualified C flags. Link commands and driver receipts retain original objects,
+order, -no-pie, exact Wild path and -lm/-ldl.
+
+hp_pad.c inserts only after the unique initial page alignment of the current
+.text.buster_checker section. Shift0 is byte-exact and introduces no marker,
+retention flag, outside padding or extra object. hp_elf.c requires zero/direct
+object semantic identity, disclosing only bounded nonsemantic metadata changes.
+For nonzero shifts it requires exact intentional prefix, hot suffix, every
+owned function (including zero size), symbol/addend/RELA/ADDRSIG translation,
+all other object sections and supported relocations. Unsupported semantics
+fail closed; alignment or instruction changes beyond the intended prefix stop.
+
+hp_linked.c requires every selected object's hot function to translate by +S
+with its identity/extent/output section retained; emit, drain and classifier
+are mandatory, plus fragment when that source exists. It checks the complete
+hot extent and linked nonrelocation bytes; only explicitly known relocation
+operand fields are masked. It records each function address/residue and each
+masked operand. Direct-normal and inside0 must BOTH match the whole qualified
+normal SHA. All objects/API/assembly/driver/raw logs/settings/zero proofs are
+hashed into a frozen snapshot. A final ready record binds its SHA and the
+normal/source-manifest identities. Later inside steps revalidate this snapshot,
+source manifest, source array, normal/zero images and toolchain before probes.
+Completion markers are written only after gates and source postchecks pass.
+
+hp_receipt.c writes complete exclusive proof/identity records and declares scope
+limits. These gates attest ELF section-header geometry and nonrelocation bytes,
+not PT_LOAD/runtime loading or correctness of numeric resolved relocation
+operands. Pinned linker/input identities, exact zero image and separate per-image
+object-preservation/semantic controls are essential additional gates. No image
+is executed by the controller; no compiler-input or runtime oracle is inferred
+from structural placement. Local synthetic support tests prove neither real
+producer compatibility nor successful hot placement of actual binaries.
+
+POTENTIAL FUTURE OPERATIONS (HELD; NOT RUN BY THIS PREPARATION)
+
+Build the C tool with the same strict local support-tool command in CONTROLS.txt.
+Each actual objects or inside operation must be its OWN invocation under the
+existing shared 9700X exclusive.sh owner/title/link protocol and <=480-second
+inner timeout; never a campaign-wide lock, manual HELD/perf setting or retry
+that overwrites retained receipts. Use a NEW task-private root for ce1/cecd.
+Arguments for the prepared CLI (all paths canonical absolute):
+
+  hp_method objects --tree SOURCE --out NEW_OBJECT_ROOT --normal QUALIFIED_NORMAL
+    --manifest QUALIFIED_FULL_SOURCE_SHA_MANIFEST
+    --flags-reference QUALIFIED_COMPILE_FLAGS_NUL
+    --sources-reference QUALIFIED_SOURCES_NUL --tc VERIFIED_OFFICIAL_TC
+    --normal-sha256 EXACT_QUALIFIED_NORMAL_SHA
+
+  hp_method inside --objects OBJECT_ROOT --shift S
+
+S is16,64,256,1024,2048; the objects operation itself proves inside0. The original
+normal image remains a separate control. The caller must externally preserve
+source/tool/harness/receipt hashes and the whole C package pin. Ready/snapshot
+records detect accidental mutation, not an adversarial rewrite of all records.
+A failed variant stays failed and its outputs remain; use new roots for any
+separately reviewed retry. All timing cells and produced compiler execution
+remain separate operations outside this controller, each separately locked.
+
+REMAINING GAPS BEFORE ANY TIMING
+
+1. Independent actual C package review and root producer-use disposition.
+2. New exact ce1/cecd 9700X normal images with official pinned TC and Wild,
+   complete source archives/manifests and qualified NUL flags/source references.
+   Existing other-host/other-mode qualification does not furnish these images.
+3. Successful direct/zero assembly controls and all actual +S hot-member proofs,
+   including every relevant function's delta/residue and section ownership.
+   A16 shift can be neutralized by later alignment or change branch/NOP bytes;
+   any such failure stops, never relabel it as successful placement.
+4. Successful zero-exit A/A/B/scalar output preservation and strict complete
+   node-report preflight on frozen SQLite and exact-pinned Lua, normal and all
+   layouts, with equal-length argv0 copies verified against their source hashes.
+   These limited object-identity checks are valid preservation controls; a
+   separate absolute runtime oracle, if requested, has separately bounded scope.
+5. Root disposition on all previous findings and current final source composition.
+   Then separately authorized balanced lower-stage/whole-process comparisons,
+   matching counts/semantics, actual durations and A/A controls. No speedup or
+   global expression coverage is claimed by trace counts or by this preparation.
